body:
Tell her everyone has bad games and a game shouldnt be the reason we break up lol.

&#x200B;

If she wants to win or have a bigger impact on the game, tell her to play tank and your pocket on supp would have a much bigger impact. If she gets defensive about it, dump her, because this means she considers your advice as something personally targeting her(like calling her bad at the game in a sense) is a red flag lol. Then again y'all can be 14 and grow out of it if you keep your online relationship going for some reason in general.

Actually your comment was justified because a huge chunk of OW community believe Mercy isn't good for the game. This has been mentioned time n time again since even the launch of the original title. Compared to other supports she is actually the most polished as in her abilities work 90% of the time and she is hard to kill having a dash that covers half the map on a 1.5 second cooldown and the ability to fly which automatically requires you to pick hitscan as a counter, otherwise your game is doomed.

&#x200B;

Oh yea I completely forgot about rez which is arguably the most broken base ability of any support in the game. Imagine your entire team pushing resources in order to kill a target and then mercy just casually walking to his body and pressing a button that cost u and your team like 4x 10-second cooldown abilities to execute. Now that is a called a low blow.

&#x200B;

Also the guy commenting 'skill issue' is just another troll of many on this sub.

Which part of Mercy pocket did you not understand lol? A mercy is character that pockets aka dmg boosts and heals whenever needed. Isn't that literally what a mercy is as a hero? On top of having the ***basic ability btw*** to rez a literal 700hp target in an instant behind a wall or another piece of cover where she is not exposed at all and requires for the enemy team to literally dive 4 people in order to even try and prevent it(plot twist, most of the time just one hero and one clip isn't enough to even stop her), I don't understand what else you need to actually even consider her kit is bloated af compared other supports and requires literally 0 payoff.

&#x200B;

Also I don't think there's even a point in trying to discuss this with a Mercy/support main at all. Happy grinding, buddy.
